    "created_at": "2025-07-16T17:21:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-07-16T17:21:47Z",
    "body": "Thanks Lea!\n\n> whether one or more options can be selected in a `<select>` has been coupled with whether the `<select>` is rendered as a dropdown or a listbox\n\nI am planning on fixing this here: https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/8189#issuecomment-2877242732\n\n> define an attribute for selecting one of the two modes (names TBB, let's use `type=\"dropdown | list\"` for the sake of this), whose default value is `auto`, which resolves to `list` if either `multiple` or `size` is specified and `dropdown` otherwise (the current behavior).\n\nThat sounds OK to me, but I am planning on making the existing size and muliple attributes work in a way that is hopefully web compatible due to this feedback: https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/8189#issuecomment-2503177401\n\n> Alternatively, this could be done via a CSS `appearance` value\n\nI don't think this is a good idea: https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12468#issuecomment-3079412845",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
