    "body": "@josepharhar gah, we crossed streams — I just edited pretty much everything in my first post to account for the CSS WG discussion today 😀 \n\nFWIW I think your proposed change, if web compatible, is a good direction _anyway_ , since `size=1` renders as a dropdown if `multiple` is not specified, so it makes the behavior more predictable. I don't see them as mutually exclusive though — given that the default `type` would be `auto`, this would just become part of how `auto` resolves to either value.",
